  "tcg-Appendix 1: Mega Evolution Pokémon ex": {
    "entry_sha256": "94f25b5577c8857d17cc86c498fa223c581752fe99a64191a2e45564e1403dfc",
    "findings": [
      {
        "class": "OMISSION",
        "note": "the source's headline contrast is that, unlike the older Mega Evolution Pokemon-EX, this card type has no special rules for playing it — notably no turn-ending rule. The entry rendered that as a deck-building remark only, so a judge cross-reading the Mega Evolution Pokemon-EX entry could carry the turn-ending rule across in the live format. Fixed: added a state line saying nothing about putting one into play ends your turn",
        "resolved": true,
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "class": "INVENTION",
        "note": "the entry described the off-ladder Evolution examples as evolving from the pre-Mega line's Stage 1; the source never gives those stages, and one of its examples in fact evolves straight from a Basic. Fixed: the line no longer asserts a specific stage",
        "resolved": true,
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
    "verdict": "findings"
  },
